Importance of Entrepreneurship
Entrepreneurship can be defined as a systematic,
purposeful and creative activity of identfying a need,
mobilising resources and organising production with a
view to delivering value to the customers, returns for
the investors and profits for the self in accordance with
the risks & uncertainities associated with business.
Entrepreneurship is important for national growth and
social development. The most common problem they
are facing is to conserve the outflow of limited national
wealth and fulfilling the demand for consumer goods
and services by locally producing them.
